.TH XRP\-TX 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
xrp\-tx \- xrp\-tx keys   < family\-seed                       \-> {"chain":"xrp","algo","address","x_address","public"} (public only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
 xrp\-tx keys   < family\-seed                       \-> {"chain":"xrp","algo","address","x_address","public"} (public only)
 xrp\-tx build  \-\-account r.. \-\-to r..|X.. (\-\-amount DROPS | \-\-sweep \-\-balance DROPS [\-\-reserve DROPS])
 xrp\-tx decode < HEX                               \-> decoded JSON
 xrp\-tx sign   \-\-tx FILE \-\-expect\-to r..|X..  < family\-seed \-> {"status":"ok","tx_blob","hash"} after a typed code on /dev/tty
 The destination tag matters: exchanges credit deposits by tag, and a payment without it is usually lost to you.
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
xrp\-tx build  \-\-account r.. \-\-to r..|X.. (\-\-amount DROPS | \-\-sweep \-\-balance DROPS [\-\-reserve DROPS])
.nf
.RS 2
              \-\-fee DROPS \-\-sequence N [\-\-last\-ledger N] [\-\-destination\-tag N]   \-> {"unsigned":HEX,"warnings":[..]}
.RE
.fi
xrp\-tx decode < HEX                               \-> decoded JSON
xrp\-tx sign   \-\-tx FILE \-\-expect\-to r..|X..  < family\-seed \-> {"status":"ok","tx_blob","hash"} after a typed code on /dev/tty
The destination tag matters: exchanges credit deposits by tag, and a payment without it is usually lost to you.
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
               \-\-fee DROPS \-\-sequence N [\-\-last\-ledger N] [\-\-destination\-tag N]   \-> {"unsigned":HEX,"warnings":[..]}
.fi
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
xrp\-tx decode < HEX                               \-> decoded JSON
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success (JSON lines may still carry status fields such as done / no_candidates).
.TP
2
Bad input, unsupported shape, or tool\-reported failure (JSON status is the detail).
.TP
3
Refused on purpose (watch\-only, policy deny, human abort, missing confirmation).
.PP
Other nonzero codes are tool\-specific; always read the last JSON status line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
See recipes/ for end\-to\-end flows. Search for xrp\-tx in recipes/*.md.
| xrp_seed | xrp\-tx keys, exit 3 \-> xrp\-tx build/sign | xrp.md |
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It opens hostile wallet files and extracts secrets: run it only sealed and offline (./blocktools run).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, docs/getting\-started.md, recipes/README.md
